"""Audioscripts (speaker, line) used by tts_dialog.py and lesson builders."""
A702 = [("E", "Hi, Tom. Thanks for your email on the recruitment companies."),
 ("T", "No problem. So which agency do we want to use? We're recruiting for two jobs at the Manchester office and one in London."),
 ("E", "I'm not sure. All Recruit has a London office, and Jones doesn't. Is that a problem?"),
 ("T", "I don't think so, Jones is bigger. And they have offices near London."),
 ("E", "Yes, that's true. But I can see that All Recruit offers a six-month guarantee on candidates."),
 ("T", "Yes, that means, if the candidate leaves the company in the first six months, All Recruit will not charge us any fees. Jones only offers a three-month guarantee."),
 ("E", "Right, and it says here All Recruit do background checks on candidates as well. Does that mean a check on job history and their use of social media, that kind of thing?"),
 ("T", "That's correct, although Jones can also do that."),
 ("E", "Ah, yes, I can see that. But All Recruit also searches for candidates on professional networking sites..."),
 ("T", "Yes, that would be useful."),
 ("E", "...and then do candidate interviews with their expert consultants. So they will do everything for us and probably find the right people."),
 ("T", "Yes, they will. The problem might be the cost."),
 ("E", "Hmm. Good point. So, All Recruit charges a fee of ten to fifteen percent of the candidate's first-year salary. So, that's around three thousand on a thirty thousand salary. That could be expensive, you're right."),
 ("T", "Well, the alternative is Jones. They charge a fixed fee of three hundred and ninety-nine pounds for their standard service. It includes advertising and selection of CVs, but obviously no interview for that fee. They can do background checks for an additional fee."),
 ("E", "OK. Maybe we just need the agency to advertise the job, check the candidate's background and then give us a list of ten candidates. We can do the interviews. I'd like to meet the candidates anyway."),
 ("T", "Yes, exactly. But first, we need to know Jones' fee for background checks. I'll phone them now."),
 ("E", "Great. If Jones are cheaper than All Recruit overall, let's use them."),
 ("T", "OK, that sounds good. I'll let you know what they say.")]

# A2+ 1.01 (updated 2026, Barcelona, bleisure). M = Marek (host), A = Alicia (events manager)
A2P_101 = [("M", "Hello and welcome back to World of Work, the podcast about how we work in 2026. Today I'm in Barcelona with Alicia Romero. Welcome, Alicia."),
 ("A", "Thanks, Marek. It's great to be here."),
 ("M", "So, let's start with this. What does an events manager do?"),
 ("A", "I manage events!"),
 ("M", "Right, the job title says it all."),
 ("A", "Exactly. I help companies plan events: conferences, product launches, team offsites, and more and more, hybrid events, with people in the room and people online."),
 ("M", "What about weddings?"),
 ("A", "No, never. Weddings are harder than business lunches! Wedding planners do those."),
 ("M", "OK. So who are your clients?"),
 ("A", "About ninety percent are businesses: tech companies, banks, start-ups. I sometimes plan private parties, but not very often."),
 ("M", "When you plan an event, where do you start?"),
 ("A", "First, I find out what the client wants: what type of event it is, and when. The timing is usually important. For example, a product launch, or welcoming new employees."),
 ("M", "And what about money?"),
 ("A", "We always talk about the budget at the first meeting. Prices are higher than they were five years ago: hotels, flights, food, everything. I try to find the best location for each event. I can't choose the most expensive hotel in Barcelona for a client with a small budget. For a cheap event, we choose the least expensive venue possible."),
 ("M", "Is anything difficult about Barcelona?"),
 ("A", "Planning an event outdoors is always the biggest challenge. In summer it's very hot here, and you can't control the weather!"),
 ("M", "What's different about your job in 2026?"),
 ("A", "Two things. First, people want to stay. The conference is on Thursday and Friday, and about half of the guests stay for the weekend. We call it bleisure, business and leisure. So now I plan the weekend too: a city tour, a boat trip, a list of good restaurants. Second, a lot of my work is online. Guests register with a QR code, an AI tool helps me with the schedule, and we stream the talks for people at home."),
 ("M", "Do clients want something special?"),
 ("A", "Always! They want an original idea. Last year, I organised a tenth anniversary party for a software company. We had the party on a rooftop with a view of the whole city, a DJ, and a 'no laptops' rule. About three hundred guests. Everyone had a great time."),
 ("M", "Was it more difficult than your usual events?"),
 ("A", "No, not really. We always have some entertainment, but we also arrange the food, now with vegan and gluten-free options, the tables and chairs, the sound system for the speeches, the livestream ..."),
 ("M", "So there are a lot of details."),
 ("A", "It's all details!"),
 ("M", "And what skills do you need?"),
 ("A", "You need to be organised, and you need to pay attention to detail. And you really need to get on with people, because the job is all about making people happy. My top priority is client satisfaction."),
 ("M", "Are any of the skills more important, or less important?"),
 ("A", "Honestly, no. You need all of them. If you love people but you can't organise, you can't do this job. If you pay attention to detail but you can't manage a budget, forget it!"),
 ("M", "That makes sense. Thanks, Alicia. Stay with us. After the break, we're going to talk about ...")]
